  "slug": "cryo-structure-34d6",
  "summary": "Generative ensemble models for proteins, antibodies, IDPs and RNA now sit beside MD-based pocket and strain analyses that treat structure as dynamic and state-dependent.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is moving from single static poses to conformational distributions with energetic or kinetic annotation. OriDynamics targets all-atom ensembles for monomers and complexes; Cadense generates antibody Fv ensembles from sequence, trained on MD-derived distributions; bAIes is extended to six structure predictors for IDP ensembles; REVEAL chains secondary-structure sampling, trRosettaRNA2, MD and Markov state modeling for HIV-1 TAR. A transition-conditioned fingerprint ranks players within rare-event corridors. Published work grounds this in physics: metadynamics maps c-MYC pockets, AIMNet2-CPCM computes ligand strain across ~8K PDB ligands, and MCCE analysis of 37 kinase cocrystals shows binding can shift protonation or tautomer states. Newer here is the breadth of ensemble generators across molecule classes, paired with explicit bound-state energetics.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-14"
}
